"""
Custom 16-level Si I/II/III model atom used by the GraphNet NLTE model.

This atom is NOT part of any released Lightweaver: it was developed as a local patch to
`lightweaver/rh_atoms.py` on the development machine. It is vendored here so the repo runs
against a stock `pip install lightweaver` instead of requiring that patched checkout.

The 16 levels are exactly the ones the network predicts departure coefficients for, in this
order -- do not reorder them, the checkpoint depends on it.

Imported by generate_database.py, api.py and the explore_tests.py plotting entry points
(run from the repo root, like the rest of the code):

    from si_atom import Si_atom_custom
    aSet = lw.RadiativeSet([..., Si_atom_custom(), ...])
"""
